## 4. Versioning Policy (operational detail)

| Axis | Format | Bumped when |
|---|---|---|
| Architecture Version | `vMAJOR.MINOR` (e.g. `v9.0`) | A new phase is designed or existing module boundaries are restructured |
| Engine Version | `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (e.g. `v9.1.0`) | Any module within the phase changes build state (new module completed, bugfix shipped) |
| Module Version | `vMAJOR.MINOR` per module (e.g. `FVG Engine v1.2`) | Internal logic changes; MAJOR bump only if contract shape changes |
| Contract Version | Stamped field inside every emitted contract instance (e.g. `contractVersion: "FVGContract-1.0"`) | Only when the contract's field set or field semantics change |

Rule: **a contract version bump forces re-validation (Gates 1–4) of every downstream consumer of that contract**, even if those consumers' own logic didn't change.

